{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D21-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"cb055a5a3465579df2c6ed3a54b43af3dba4f372739f4769d940f1e170228226\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers a cloth, but A3's 'You must be thrilled' replaces encouragement with mockery.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's spreading paint; A5 barely uses B4's request to remove blue paint.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 wants practical cleanup, while A3 mainly ridicules B rather than helping.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 complains about the afternoon without developing the helpfulness or visibly increasing fury.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's painted sofa and B2's carpet establish an immediately playable domestic accident.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Wonderful coverage' is compact; A5's afternoon metaphor displaces the cleanup.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 55\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You've spilled paint on my sofa. Stay there; I'll get a cloth. We can fix this.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's on the carpet too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep blotting. You're doing well. That carpet was my birthday present.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The cloth's spreading it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're right. Good catch. Take my clean shirt. I am absolutely furious, but you are not tackling this alone.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A must keep providing sincere help and encouragement as the same interaction makes A increasingly furious.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Sarcastic politeness can sound supportive while actually withdrawing encouragement and care.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 mocks B's satisfaction; revised A3 praises blotting and A5 supplies a shirt despite explicit fury.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative handles accidental damage through practical rescue; D21-single-b supports an indecisive passenger under financial pressure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the paint accident to restore simultaneous support and anger. Second internal pass: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 encourage through fury), logic 5 (B4's spreading cloth causes A5's shirt), relationship 4 (B2/B4 report worsening damage), heightening 4 (A5 sacrifices clothing), specificity 5 (A1 sofa cleanup), brevity 4 (A5 is direct but explicit): 92/100. Five spoken ABABA turns and the word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 names fury directly; performance must also convey its increase without making the encouragement sarcastic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D21-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"2fbce0a3cf72a7df5ca943a87acc34f8e5e26d0b28e53514f86306f26fe1b5f0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 personify the meter sarcastically, with little sincere encouragement or increasing fury.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 prompts parking pressure in A3, but A5's 'relationship trial' adds little to B4's relocation request.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 express indecision; A's actual support remains largely the initial driving offer.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the meter joke without increasing sacrifice or anger after B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes lunch and driving; A3 supplies a credible parking constraint.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'relationship trial' feels constructed around the meter rather than A's sincere objective.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 51\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Choose the birthday lunch you really want. I'll drive.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The seaside place. We'd lose your deposit here.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Forty pounds wasted. Fine. You love the sea; let's make a day of it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've booked it. They need another forty now.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Another forty? Eighty pounds before a bloody sandwich. Give me the number. You're getting your sea view. Ask for a window; you deserve one.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A continues helping and encouraging B while successive costs make A's speech increasingly furious.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Passive aggression would make the encouragement a disguised attack on B instead of sustaining the promised treat.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 endorses B2's seaside choice despite the lost deposit; A5 protests the doubled cost yet actively secures B4's booking and encourages a window request.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"D21-single-a sacrifices possessions during an accident; this birthday chauffeur voluntarily sustains a treat as B's choice doubles the immediate expense.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the birthday outing so B4 adds an unavoidable second payment rather than an easily solved cash shortage. Separate internal reread: fidelity 4 (A3's restrained complaint grows into A5's angry arithmetic while help continues), logic 5 (B2 loses the deposit; B4 doubles the outlay), relationship 4 (B chooses and books the desired treat), heightening 4 (A5 funds the new commitment while pushing for a better seat), specificity 5 (A1 birthday drive, B2 seaside reservation), brevity 4 (A5's sandwich complaint arises from the actual expense): 86/100. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, and hard gates pass; this is model review only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's 'Fine' and A5's window encouragement must remain sincere; the text gives anger a concrete cause but delivery still controls whether support sounds barbed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D22-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a49c538c9db82c4c37811149967671959028a8e1b8afa39f29af055c7194de96\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 prices a favor and A3 renegotiates it, but A5 labels negotiation instead of making another proposal.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's five minutes causes A3's lower price; B4's cash offer gets only an abstract response.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 challenges disproportionate terms and B4 offers a simpler transaction.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 invokes friendship without attaching a new condition or consequence to B4's payment offer.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's ladder and station lifts establish concrete neighborly bargaining.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's public garden praise is economical and characterful; A5 is more explanatory.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 76\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll lend you the ladder for two lifts to the station.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I only need it for five minutes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One lift, then. And tell your wife my roses have improved.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can I just pay you?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Five pounds. Three if you say we're still friends when you hand it over.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns practical favors and emotional reassurance alike into terms that can be offered and exchanged.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary haggling concerns the ladder's price alone rather than treating friendship itself as negotiable consideration.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 and A3 bargain over use; revised A5 gives a cash discount specifically for reassurance about friendship.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This scene trades a useful object for favors and affection; D22-single-b negotiates the settlement of an apology.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the neighborly ladder setting and replaced A5's commentary with an actual counteroffer. Second internal pass: fidelity 5 (A5 prices reassurance), logic 5 (B4 cash becomes A5 cash terms), relationship 4 (B seeks a simpler payment), heightening 4 (friendship enters the bargain), specificity 5 (A1 ladder/lifts), brevity 4 (A5 compact conditional offer): 92/100. ABABA and word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The monetary figures are illustrative, and the affectionate discount should sound sincerely important to A.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D22-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f1f9833f8c367b450edeb23ce67fc1865a9bdb920a6d4198fac1772979b6d5ba\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 conditions acceptance and A3 demands a warranty, clearly commercializing the apology.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's sorrow, but A5 introduces a refund clause without any established loss or payment.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek recognition of remorse, but the unknown offense limits their practical options.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds contractual language to B4's sincerity without making its consequences clear.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an apology but never identifies the incident, relationship, or desired remedy.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'I need a warranty' is concise and follows the transactional attitude.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll accept your apology for missing my birthday if I get first choice of Christmas dates.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Mum already expects me Christmas Day.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Boxing Day, then. In exchange, I'll tell her I'm no longer hurt.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'd rather you actually stopped being hurt.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay through New Year and I'll mean it. But you get to choose when I forgive you.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A negotiates the acceptance of an apology, the expression of hurt, and the feeling itself as exchangeable concessions.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Restitution would seek compensation for a concrete loss; this A also prices emotional recovery and offers control over forgiveness.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 trades a declaration of recovery for B2's available holiday; B4's demand for genuine recovery makes A5 negotiate the sincerity and timing of forgiveness.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"D22-single-a trades a ladder for favors and reassurance; this sibling scene bargains over holiday access and whether reconciliation is merely announced or actually felt.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the blender dispute with an illustrative missed-birthday and family-holiday negotiation to move beyond ordinary restitution. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 trades expressed hurt and A5 genuine forgiveness), logic 5 (B2 changes the date; B4 changes the emotional terms), relationship 4 (B has a competing family commitment and wants real reconciliation), heightening 4 (A5 prices actual recovery with a longer stay), specificity 4 (A1 birthday and Christmas establish family stakes), brevity 4 (A5's timing concession is an active offer): 90/100. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, and hard gates pass; no human or live review is claimed.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's belief that a longer visit can purchase emotional recovery is deliberately unreasonable; it must sound like a sincere proposal rather than knowingly theatrical punishment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D23-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f28c138ced5d74de2744fe531ca413be583ea2fec5e0d59821c16b9c76cd69e1\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 agrees to help but supplies moral support; A3 and A5 keep redefining the promise to avoid carrying.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's sofa prompts A3's encouragement of its carrier; B4's 'muscle' directly supplies A5's jaw reinterpretation.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 needs physical help and B4 invokes A's prior promise, tightening the obligation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 absorbs B4's explicit muscle requirement into the same self-serving form of assistance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes moving help and B2 identifies the sofa that needs carrying.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's jaw claim is brief and earned by B4's wording, though deliberately cheeky.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes, I'll help you move the sofa. I'll take the cushions.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They're sewn on. We have to lift together.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Absolutely. You lift; I'll say when. Together.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I need another person underneath it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Agreed. I'll book someone on your phone. Then I can give both of you the same countdown.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A agrees to each concrete requirement while redefining participation so A keeps the effortless supervisory role.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple refusal would decline lifting; A instead claims each favorable substitute fulfills B's requested cooperation.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 accepts B2's 'together' as synchronized instruction, and A5 accepts B4's extra lifter by booking someone else through B's phone.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative moves from selecting light work to supervising hired labor; D23-single-b converts dog hosting into receiving company while its owner retains care.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the jaw pun with successive practical attempts to exempt A from lifting. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1, A3 and A5 agree while assigning A the easiest role), logic 5 (B2 blocks detachable cushions; B4 requires an actual second lifter), relationship 4 (B repeatedly specifies the help needed), heightening 4 (A5 adds outside labor while preserving command), specificity 5 (A1 sofa, B2 sewn cushions), brevity 4 (A3's 'Together' expresses the reinterpretation economically): 92/100. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, and hard gates pass. Original firstPass remains unchanged despite the supplied later rejection.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Using B's phone implies that B will manage the booking expense; the scene does not establish payment, so the primary benefit to A is avoiding physical work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D23-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0525c18ab80e10cb94411009e0bd5196e576a3ca9eb81f155ab2b1beead08027\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 agrees and A3 twists 'look after,' but A5 abandons agreement to blame B's wording.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains the office through a strained spatial pun; A5 acknowledges B4's house without adapting the arrangement.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 pursue actual dog care, but A's benefit from trailing the dog remains unclear.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's complaint about specifications does not develop a new favorable interpretation of B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's weekend dog care and B2's office are concrete, though A3's position is awkward to play.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'from behind' and A5's 'viewing location' prioritize wordplay over the agreement.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 57\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes, I'll look after your dog during your kitchen repairs. Bring him over after his walk.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He needs to stay overnight too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Absolutely. You can use my guest room and handle breakfast. I'll have company without getting up.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He'll wake you barking for his six o'clock walk.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Agreed, we'd better prevent that. Set your alarm for five thirty.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A accepts increasingly specific dog-care requirements while interpreting the arrangement as convenient company with all inconvenient care retained by B.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A negotiated compromise would openly limit A's promise; A presents B doing the work as wholehearted fulfillment of that promise.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 answers B2's overnight requirement by accommodating the owner as caretaker, and A5 turns B4's warning about barking into an earlier alarm for B.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"D23-single-a recruits outside lifting help while A supervises; this alternative welcomes B and the dog for companionship while protecting A's mornings.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified kitchen repairs so B can credibly stay with the dog, and replaced A3's ordinary concession with a favorable reinterpretation. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 assigns breakfast to B and A5 protects A's sleep), logic 5 (B2 requires overnight arrangements; B4's six o'clock barking causes a five-thirty alarm), relationship 4 (B needs accommodation and explains the dog's routine), heightening 4 (A5 advances B's wake-up to prevent A's), specificity 5 (A1 repairs and dog care), brevity 4 (A5 makes the self-serving solution concrete): 92/100. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, and hard gates pass; model reread only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A supplies real accommodation, but every spoken agreement frames that contribution around A's convenience and preserves B's care duties.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D24-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a0d09c3eaa706e9cb7e5abcbc4f081817f2f4809b0f36a87607312822212f9d6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 expands two missing biscuits into an operation; A3 and A5 treat confession and hunger as further evidence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's immediate confession becomes A3's training evidence; B4's hunger becomes A5's recruitment method.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 accepts responsibility and B4 offers a mundane motive, attempting to close the inquiry.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns B4's ordinary hunger into an organized recruitment system beyond the office tin.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 names two office biscuits, giving actors a trivial, concrete incident.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's quick-confession inference is economical; A5's 'goes higher' is familiar but causally earned.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 95\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Two office biscuits are missing. We've got an organised operation.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I ate them.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A confession this quick suggests training.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I was hungry.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then they're recruiting through hunger. This goes higher than the biscuit tin.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats each small explanation of missing biscuits as fresh evidence of a larger organized problem.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic conspiracy talk could ignore incoming facts; this exchange builds its larger theory from B's particular explanations.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 specifically uses the speed of B2's confession, and A5 specifically turns B4's hunger into recruitment.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Here A enlarges a coworker's admitted action into external organization; D24-single-b absorbs A's own error into the alleged system.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly because both attempted explanations materially enlarge the same theory. Internal rereading confirms 95/100 and all hard gates without changing the dialogue.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The conspiracy framing is one expression of a broader card and should not become its only interpretation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D24-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"acd90a6333ddb547e144668a80cf369f06f72f808b505b64cde1cf0204def6fd\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 links two delays into deliberate interference; A3 and A5 keep turning minor email facts into systemic evidence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's draft status, and A5 uses B4's personal responsibility, although 'sending stage' is vague.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 diagnoses the missing email and B4 identifies the action A has omitted.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends the supposed system into A's own behavior when B4 removes an external explanation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a slow lift and late email; B2 makes the email problem playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'recruited me' is short and depends on B4's correction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Nobody received my meeting email. This office has stopped communicating.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's in your drafts. You forgot to send it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And nobody noticed. Our entire communication system depends on my memory.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll send it. Go and have your lunch.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Now you're covering communications while I'm absent. We need a succession plan before I take a sandwich.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats a minor personal omission and its easy repair as evidence of increasingly serious organizational fragility.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoiding blame would deny forgetting; A accepts that fact and expands its significance into an office-wide problem.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 accepts B2's forgotten send as dependence on A's memory; B4's helpful cover becomes A5's evidence that routine lunch requires succession planning.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"D24-single-a interprets a coworker's confession as conspiracy; this alternative includes A's own error and a colleague's helpful solution in a diagnosis of institutional fragility.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the office email but replaced the vague sending-stage inference and repeated correction with practical cover. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 enlarge mundane facts into systemic problems), logic 5 (B2's omission becomes memory dependence; B4's lunch cover becomes succession), relationship 4 (B wants to send the email and release A for lunch), heightening 4 (A5 makes a meal contingent on organizational planning), specificity 4 (A1 meeting email establishes the shared task), brevity 4 (A5's sandwich follows B4's lunch): 90/100. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, and hard gates pass; original firstPass is preserved.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final succession language is exaggerated, but A's concern must remain sincere rather than a knowingly grand description of routine cover.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D25-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d19698499269ffc2fef2bbe7e15663d23c6e08b0f6e06adbcd5752cf726189fa\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 requests holding, A3 adds screws, and A5 adds loading and another shelf until B has most of the installation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2 holding the shelf enables A3's screw request; B4's completion and invitation enable A5's next favors.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 willingly helps and B4 actively offers further assistance, allowing cooperative task capture.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands a completed installation into loading it and starting the matching shelf.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes holding a shelf while screws are located, a clear physical task.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Just the books' minimizes a growing workload without explanatory dialogue.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you hold this shelf bracket against the holes? It keeps slipping.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Briefly. I'm dressed for work.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you turn that top screw once? Then you can let go.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's holding. The other screws are already lined up.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Just tighten those, then? And slide the shelf onto it to check. I'll get your coat.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A subdivides awkward shelf mounting into small favors until B performs the fastening and fitting while A supplies only peripheral help.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Direct delegation would assign the installation upfront; A secures each small operation through the helper's preceding progress.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks only for holding, A3 offers a single screw turn as release from holding, and A5 uses B4's aligned screws to obtain the remaining fastening and fitting.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative grows an installation favor around B's work deadline; D25-single-b uses B's corrective expertise to transfer the delicate preparation of a wedding bouquet.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept shelf installation, gave B an independent need to leave, and removed the jump to an entire second shelf. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1, A3 and A5 transfer almost all mounting through small requests), logic 5 (B2's brevity constraint prompts a release tactic; B4's aligned screws prompt finishing), relationship 4 (B is dressed for work and reports useful progress), heightening 4 (A5 acquires fastening and fitting while offering the coat), specificity 5 (A1 bracket and holes establish the awkward task), brevity 4 (A3's 'once' makes the favor sound tiny): 92/100. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, and hard gates pass; original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The holes are already prepared, so the difficult task demonstrated is mounting the shelf, not the entire process of planning and drilling an installation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D25-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"36623deee56f49b21d3580f3551fc2e36eb1cd424e315d898db29ac3faf46dcd\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 starts with a tiny favor, but A3 immediately assigns fifty envelopes instead of accumulating small requests.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's completion supplies A3's pattern, and B4's 'one' supplies A5's reinterpretation.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 helps and B4 objects to the expanded commitment, giving B a credible boundary.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 declares B trained but adds no incremental favor after B4 resists the bulk assignment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's envelope and handwriting compliment establish a concrete, playable request.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'One demonstration' is compact, but its wit belongs more to reinterpreting an agreement.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 67\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you pinch these bouquet stems together? My wedding ribbon keeps sliding.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've got them. You need wire underneath.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"